README-X68K -- programs for the Sharp X68000's personal-window systemOS-9/X68000 ran on Sharp's X68000 with a windowing system of its own, the"personal window" (PW/X), reached through the /win device.  These twoprograms were written for it in 1991-92.  They are untested: there is noX68000 and no /win here.  Started anyway, x9eyes answers `PwCreateMaperror' and setbgptn `can't open /win'.  Both need cio.  x9eyes     xeyes for the personal window: two eyes that follow the             pointer, in a resizable window.  -t<tick> sets how often it             redraws; -g<width>x<height> sets the size.  Version 1.04,             1992-12-10.  setbgptn   sets the window system's background pattern from a file of             16 lines of 16 characters: a space for a clear dot, anything             else for a set one.  The archive has four: BLACK.BGP,             BLOCK.BGP, DEFAULT.BGP and X.BGP.The archives ship whole in CMDS/archives, as their terms require.x9eyes.doc: "(1) Please do not change the contents of the originalarchive.  (2) Please tell the author, where possible, where it has beendistributed."  PwLib.doc, for the library both are built on: "Feel freeto redistribute provided that 1. the author's credits are not removed,and 2. the composition of the archive is not changed -- additions by thedistributor are allowed."  This file is a distributor's addition.Their documentation is Japanese, in Shift-JIS, which this disk cannotcarry as text; it is inside the archives, unchanged.The archives are the author's 2018-09-11 re-release of the 1991-92 work.setbgptn's carries the 1991 library; x9eyes's carries the library asre-released in 2018, and its binary is the one shipped here.